[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 7s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  An agent skill is a modular package containing instructions, knowledge, and scripts, enabling an AI agent to p...\u001b[m\r\n  In AI coding assistants and autonomous agent systems (such as Antigravity, Claude Code, and modern agent\u001b[K\r\n  frameworks), \u001b[1mAgent Skills\u001b[m are modular, reusable packages of instructions, runbooks, scripts, and domain\u001b[K\r\n  knowledge that teach an agent how to execute specialized workflows reliably.\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### 1. The Core Concept\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  If an AI agent is a versatile developer, a \u001b[1mSkill\u001b[m is an on-demand standard operating procedure (SOP) or\r\n  \"playbook.\"\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Instead of relying solely on general training data or trying to guess project-specific steps, the agent refers\r\n  to the skill to follow exact, battle-tested procedures (e.g., \u001b[3mdeploying via Terraform\u001b[m, \u001b[3mhandling database\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[3mmigrations\u001b[m, \u001b[3msetting up FFI bindings\u001b[m, or \u001b[3mrunning accessibility audits\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  ───"]
[0.000, "o", "───\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### 2. How Skills Work: Progressive Disclosure\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  One of the main challenges in agent design is context window management. If all project documentation and\r\n  instructions were loaded into every prompt, the context window would quickly fill up with irrelevant text.\r\n\u001b[K\n  Skills solve this using \u001b[1mprogressive disclosure\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[4C\u001b[38;5;252m[User Prompt] ──▶ Agent matches prompt against short skill descriptions\u001b[m\n\u001b[71D\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[7b\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\u001b[10D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[4A\u001b[10C\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[11b\u001b[m\n\n\n\n\u001b[22D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.015, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 7s\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[37m  An agent skill is a modular package containing instructions, knowledge, and scripts, enabling an AI agent to p...\u001b[m\r\n  In AI coding assistants and autonomous agent systems (such as Antigravity, Claude Code, and modern agent\r\n  frameworks), \u001b[1mAgent Skills\u001b[m are modular, reusable packages of instructions, runbooks, scripts, and domain\r\n  knowledge that teach an agent how to execute specialized workflows reliably.\r\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m### 1. The Core Concept\u001b[m\r\n\n  If an AI agent is a versatile developer, a \u001b[1mSkill\u001b[m is an on-demand standard operating procedure (SOP) or\r\n  \"playbook.\"\r\n\n  Instead of relying solely on general training data or trying to guess project-specific steps, the agent refers\r\n  to the skill to follow exact, battle-tested procedures (e.g., \u001b[3mdeploying via Terraform\u001b[m, \u001b[3mhandling database\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[3mmigrations\u001b[m, \u001b[3msetting up FFI bindings\u001b[m, or \u001b[3mrunning accessibility audits\u001b[m).\r\n  ──────\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "  \u001b[1m### 2. How Skills Work: Progressive Disclosure\u001b[m\r\n\n  One of the main challenges in agent design is context window management. If all project documentation and\r\n  instructions were loaded into every prompt, the context window would quickly fill up with irrelevant text.\r\n\n  Skills solve this using \u001b[1mprogressive disclosure\u001b[m:\n\n\u001b[45D\u001b[38;5;252m[User Prompt] ──▶ Agent matches prompt against short skill descriptions\u001b[m\n\u001b[71D\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[24X\u001b[24C│\u001b[m\n\u001b[25D\u001b[38;5;252m    \u001b[m\r\n⣾  \u001b[90mLoading...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: You can switch conversations with /resume.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────"]
