[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[27AIf an AI agent is a versatile developer, a \u001b[1mSkill\u001b[m is an on-demand standard operating procedure (SOP) or\r\n  \"playbook.\"\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Instead of relying solely on general training data or trying to guess project-specific steps, the agent refers\r\n  to the skill to follow exact, battle-tested procedures (e.g., \u001b[3mdeploying via Terraform\u001b[m, \u001b[3mhandling database\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[3mmigrations\u001b[m, \u001b[3msetting up FFI bindings\u001b[m, or \u001b[3mrunning accessibility audits\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### 2. How Skills Work: Progressive Disclosure\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  One of the main challenges in agent design is context window management. If all project documentation and\r\n  instructions were loaded into every prompt, the context window would quickly fill up with irrelevant text.\r\n\u001b[K\n  Skills solve this using \u001b[1mprogressive disclosure\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[4C\u001b[38;5;252m[User Prompt] ──▶ Agent matches prompt against short skill descriptions\u001b[m\n\u001b[71D\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[24X\u001b[24C│\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\b\u001b[38;5;252m▼ (Matches?)\u001b[m\n\u001b[18D\u001b[3"]
[0.000, "o", "8;5;252mLoads full SKILL.md & runs helper scripts on-demand\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mLightweight Indexing\u001b[m: By default, only the skill’s \u001b[94mname\u001b[m and \u001b[94mdescription\u001b[m (from its YAML metadata) are exposed\r\n  to the agent.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mOn-Demand Loading\u001b[m: When your prompt matches what the skill does, the agent dynamically reads the full \u001b[94mSKILL.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mmd\u001b[m instructions and any relevant reference files.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mExec\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\u001b[7D\u001b[?2026l"]
