[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[27AOne of the main challenges in agent design is context window management. If all project documentation and\r\n  instructions were loaded into every prompt, the context window would quickly fill up with irrelevant text.\r\n\u001b[K\n  Skills solve this using \u001b[1mprogressive disclosure\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[4C\u001b[38;5;252m[User Prompt] ──▶ Agent matches prompt against short skill descriptions\u001b[m\n\u001b[71D\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[24X\u001b[24C│\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\b\u001b[38;5;252m▼ (Matches?)\u001b[m\n\u001b[18D\u001b[38;5;252mLoads full SKILL.md & runs helper scripts on-demand\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mLightweight Indexing\u001b[m: By default, only the skill’s \u001b[94mname\u001b[m and \u001b[94mdescription\u001b[m (from its YAML metadata) are exposed\r\n  to the agent.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mOn-Demand Loading\u001b[m: When your prompt matches what the skill does, the agent dynamically reads the full \u001b[94mSKILL.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mmd\u001b[m instructions and any relevant reference files.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mExecution\u001b[m: The agent follows the defined steps and executes any bundled helper scripts.\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### "]
[0.000, "o", "3. Structure of a Skill\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  A typical skill lives as a directory (for example, inside \u001b[94m.agents/skills/<skill-name>/\u001b[m):\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[4C\u001b[38;5;252mskills/<skill-name>/\u001b[m\n\u001b[20D\u001b[38;5;252m├── SKILL.md \u001b[9b# Entry point: metadata + step-by-step instructions\u001b[m\r\n\t\u001b[38;5;252mscripts/ \u001b[9b# Optional: Executable scripts/tools for complex commands\u001b[m\r\n\t\u001b[38;5;252mre\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n⢿ \n\n\n\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[4A\u001b[8C\u001b[38;5;252mferences/   \u001b[m\n\n\n\n\u001b[20D\u001b[?2026l"]
