[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A  instructions were loaded into every prompt, the context window would quickly fill up with irrelevant text.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\n  Skills solve this using \u001b[1mprogressive disclosure\u001b[m:\n\n\u001b[45D\u001b[38;5;252m[User Prompt] ──▶ Agent matches prompt against short skill descriptions\u001b[m\n\u001b[71D\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[24X\u001b[24C│\u001b[m\n\u001b[25D\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[24X\u001b[24C▼ (Matches?)\u001b[m\n\u001b[36D\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[18X\u001b[18CLoads full SKILL.md & runs helper scripts on-demand\u001b[m\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mLightweight Indexing\u001b[m: By default, only the skill’s \u001b[94mname\u001b[m and \u001b[94mdescription\u001b[m (from its YAML metadata) are exposed\r\n  to the agent.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mOn-Demand Loading\u001b[m: When your prompt matches what the skill does, the agent dynamically reads the full \u001b[94mSKILL.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mmd\u001b[m instructions and any relevant reference files.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mExecution\u001b[m: The agent follows the defined steps and executes any bundled helper scripts.\r\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m### 3. Structure of a Skill\u001b[m\r\n\n  A typical skill lives as a directory (for example, inside \u001b[9"]
